  "parameter_metadata": {},
  "narrative": {
    "key_bets": [
      "Electromagnetic launcher can accelerate macroscopic projectiles to 60 km/s at commercial scale (15-30× extrapolation from existing railguns at 2-4 km/s)",
      "Proprietary multi-cavity 'amplifier' target design achieves 200-1000× fusion gain, versus NIF's current world record of ~4×",
      "Flowing liquid lithium curtains (1 m thick) can simultaneously serve as first wall, blanket, tritium breeder, and structural protection while surviving repetitive blast loading",
      "Tritium breeding ratio of 1.8 is achievable (independently validated by TÜV SÜD UK), enabling 25 kg/year surplus and fleet deployment without tritium banks",
      "Mass production of precision multi-cavity amplifier targets at 1.5-4.3 million units/year is economically feasible",
      "Sub-Hz repetition rate (0.033-0.1 Hz) is sufficient because high gain compensates for low shot frequency",
      "Driver operational lifetime (bore erosion, sabot wear, capacitor cycling) can sustain ~1.3 × 10⁸ shots over 40-year plant life"
    ],
    "eliminated_costs": [
      "Superconducting magnets entirely eliminated — no HTS tape, cryostats, or current leads (removes 30-50% of typical tokamak reactor plant cost)",
      "Precision beam optics absent — no final optics survivability concern that plagues laser IFE (TRL ~2 challenge avoided)",
      "Hohlraum per-target cost eliminated (saves $1k-$10k/target vs indirect-drive laser ICF)",
      "Vessel replacement avoided — liquid lithium curtain protects structural walls for plant lifetime",
      "Plasma disruption mitigation hardware unnecessary — no plasma to disrupt"
    ],
    "novel_costs": [
      "Electromagnetic gun driver at 60 km/s / 100 MJ class — no industrial or defense analogue exists, genuinely uncharacterized CAS22 item",
      "Per-shot consumables structure: 1.5-4.3 million precision amplifier targets/year plus projectiles, a recurring cost with no conventional plant cost model analogue",
      "Flowing liquid lithium curtain engineering — pump power, reactive-metal containment, blast-loading survival of fluid geometry, all with no operating-plant basis",
      "Driver operational lifetime as a recurring cost (barrel bore erosion, sabot degradation, capacitor replacement) with Pearson -0.134 LCOE correlation exceeding driver capital cost impact",
      "Target positioning/injection system capable of precision delivery at 0.033-0.1 Hz synchronized with hypervelocity projectile arrival"
    ],
    "risks": [
      {
        "description": "Electromagnetic gun capital cost is completely uncharacterized — 15-30× velocity extrapolation from existing railguns with no published analogue; FLARE pivot (Sept 2025) is indirect evidence driver cost exceeded viability threshold",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Target gain of 200-1000× has never been experimentally demonstrated; Machine 3 achieved only ~50 neutrons at 6.5 km/s, and Machine 4 (60 km/s) was cancelled February 2025 before testing the claim",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Primary commercial champion (First Light Fusion) abandoned the projectile approach in September 2025 in favor of pulsed-power FLARE, leaving no active pursuer of pure projectile ICF",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Driver operational lifetime under 60 km/s bore erosion, sabot stress, and repetitive capacitor cycling is unknown; plausible range spans 4 orders of magnitude (10⁴ to 10⁹ shots), with stronger LCOE correlation than capital cost",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Flowing liquid lithium curtain is doubly load-bearing (first wall + sole tritium breeder); if unviable, both the vessel-lifetime advantage and TBR 1.8 advantage collapse together, forcing fallback to solid blanket with TBR ~1.05-1.15",
        "severity": "high"
      },
      {
        "description": "Target fabrication cost at 1.5-4.3M units/year is proprietary with no mass-manufacturing analogue; if targets contain gold or other exotic materials, per-shot cost could become prohibitive",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Conflicting public rep rate figures (0.011-0.1 Hz) span a 10× range, propagating linearly into power output and capital amortization uncertainty",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Chamber clearing time for liquid Li curtain after blast is unknown; may impose a cliff-edge constraint preventing rep-rate compensation for gain shortfall",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "Tritium byproduct revenue (~$750M/year at current $30,000/g scarcity pricing) is structurally self-eroding — fleet-scale deployment collapses the price, so the revenue cannot be relied upon as a base-case LCOE credit",
        "severity": "medium"
      },
      {
        "description": "NearStar MTIF is taxonomically closer to MIF (magnetized fuel, D-D preference) than pure projectile ICF, leaving First Light Fusion as the sole historical champion — and FLF has now exited the approach",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ]
  },
